  "final_text": "Here's a summary and analysis of the data you've provided, which appears to be a dataset of rides with metrics like average ride time (in minutes), number of rides, and spending per ride (pay_per_use_spend) for different weeks.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcca **Summary of the Dataset**\n\n#### **Total Rows:**\n- **199 rows** of data (weeks from 2024-W34 to 2026-W40)\n\n#### **Key Metrics:**\n- **Rides per week:** Varies from **1 to 7 rides**\n- **Average ride time (avg_min):** Ranges from **3.1 minutes to 11.7 minutes**\n- **Pay per use spend (pay_per_use_spend):** Ranges from **$1.59 to $15.97**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcc8 **Trend Analysis**\n\n#### **1. Rides per Week:**\n- **Most frequent:** Weeks with **2 or 3 rides** (common across all years)\n- **Peak weeks:** Weeks with **6 or 7 rides** (e.g., 2025-W08, 2026-W28)\n- **Lowest activity:** Weeks with **1 ride** (common in many weeks)\n\n#### **2. Average Ride Time (avg_min):**\n- **Shortest rides:** Weeks with **3.1 to 4.0 minutes** (e.g., 2025-W35, 2024-W34)\n- **Longest rides:** Weeks with **10.3 to 11.7 minutes** (e.g., 2024-W37, 2025-W07)\n- **Average ride time:** Generally around **6 to 7 minutes**, with some weeks showing longer or shorter durations.\n\n#### **3. Pay per Use Spend (pay_per_use_spend):**\n- **Lowest spending:** Weeks with **$1.59 to $2.54** (e.g., 2025-W35, 2024-W38)\n- **Highest spending:** Weeks with **$15.43 to $15.97** (e.g., 2025-W08, 2026-W28)\n- **Average spending:** Around **$4 to $8 per ride**, with some weeks showing higher or lower spending.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcca **Key Observations**\n\n1. **Weeks with high ride counts (6\u20137 rides):**\n   - These weeks tend to have **higher pay_per_use_spend** (e.g., 2025-W08, 2026-W28)\n   - These weeks also have **moderate to long average ride times** (e.g., 8.3 minutes)\n\n2. **Weeks with low ride counts (1\u20132 rides):**\n   - These weeks often have **lower pay_per_use_spend** (e.g., 2024-W38, 2025-W35)\n   - These weeks also have **shorter or longer ride times** (e.g., 3.1 minutes or 11.7 minutes)\n\n3. **Seasonal or weekly patterns:**\n   - There's no clear seasonal pattern, but some weeks show **higher activity** (e.g., 2025-W08, 2026-W28)\n   - Some weeks show **very low activity** (e.g., 2024-W38, 2025-W35)\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccc **Top Weeks by Pay per Use Spend**\n| Week         | Pay per Use Spend |\n|--------------|-------------------|\n| 2025-W08     | $15.43            |\n| 2026-W28     | $15.58            |\n| 2025-W29     | $10.12            |\n| 2026-W28     | $15.58            |\n| 2025-W46     | $15.97            |\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccc **Top Weeks by Ride Count**\n| Week         | Rides |\n|--------------|-------|\n| 2025-W08     | 6     |\n| 2026-W28     | 7     |\n| 2026-W29     | 1     |\n| 2025-W46     | 6     |\n| 2026-W38     | 5     |\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccc **Top Weeks by Average Ride Time**\n| Week         | Avg Min |\n|--------------|---------|\n| 2024",
